      "math_academy_id": "q-42997",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Let $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ be square matrices. If $A=B\\cdot C,$  $|B|=9$ and $|{C}^{-1}|=-3$, find $|A|.$",
      "worked_solution": "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nAlso, given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $M,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({M}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(M)}.\n$$\n\nSince $|C|=\\frac{1}{|{C}^{-1}|}$, we get $|C|=-\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|B|\\cdot |C| \\\\  & =9\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
